<title>USA: Lower River Authority, Texas, sets $205 mln deal.</title>
<headline>Lower River Authority, Texas, sets $205 mln deal.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Lower Colorado River Authority, Texas, plans to sell a $205 million bond deal on Nov 20, a market source said Friday.</p>
<p>The deal comprises $204.2 million junier lien refunding revenue bonds and $1 million priority refunding revenue bonds.</p>
<p>The sale is slated for 1100 EST.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
